  regular expression; any matching line passes.\n\n  concepts:\n    - concept: configured greeting\n      block: given\n      service: greeter\n      references:\n      - file: greeting-config\n      does: >-\n        Write the declared greeting configuration file, greeter.yaml in\n        the run directory, as a YAML mapping whose greeting is the step's\n        quoted text, before the command runs.\n    - concept: a role runs a command\n      block: when\n      service: greeter\n      references:\n      - command: greet\n      does: >-\n        Run the declared greet command as a process once in the run\n        directory, with the words of the step's quoted command line after\n        its first word, greet, as its arguments, and keep its exit code\n        and its standard output lines.\n    - concept: exit code\n      block: then\n      service: greeter\n      references:\n      - command: greet\n      does: >-\n        Compare the kept exit code of the greet command with the step's\n        whole number.\n    - concept: standard output\n      block: then\n      service: greeter\n      references:\n      - command: greet\n      does: >-\n        Match the step's pattern, a regular expression taken as the rest\n        of the step after \"stdout matches\", against each kept standard\n        output line of the greet command; the step passes when any line\n        matches.\n","numLines":90,"startLine":1,"totalLines":90}}}
